// Title: graphix fmt refuses a statement list whose last statement ends in `;`
// and has a comment line below it (file level, a block, a seq body alike).
// Command: graphix fmt --stdout design/review-2026-10-26/repro/tests-expr-fmt-trailing-semi-below.gx
// Expected: the file printed back unchanged (it parses and checks).
// Observed: "formatter bug: the formatted text lost or moved a comment or an
// attribute", exit 1. The parser hangs the `// end` lines on `let b`'s
// Decorations::below (commented: Slot::End), and pretty_items /
// pretty_file_items print `below` only for the LAST item, which is the
// trailing `;`'s NoOp.
let f = |x| {
    println(x);
    println(x);
    // done
};
let b = f(2);
// end
